WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.504 --> 00:00:03.886
Edward's first day as a pauper had not gone as he expected.

2
00:00:03.946 --> 00:00:05.648
How did Tom spend that same day?

3
00:00:05.728 --> 00:00:13.873
Left alone in Edward's room, Tom admired himself in the mirror and played with the prince's sword.

4
00:00:32.216 --> 00:00:36.437
"I wish Julian could see me dressed up like this," Tom thought, grinning.

5
00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:39.498
"I look like a real prince!"

6
00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:45.540
He sat on all the chairs and bounced on the bed.

7
00:00:49.581 --> 00:00:52.341
He knocked on the suit of armor but didn't dare to try it on.

8
00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:57.983
After half an hour, he was bored and lonely.

9
00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:01.484
He was also beginning to worry.

10
00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.536
"Where's Prince Edward?"

11
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:05.417
he thought.

12
00:01:05.437 --> 00:01:11.098
"If anyone catches me wearing his clothes, I'll be locked up in prison forever.

13
00:01:11.118 --> 00:01:13.459
I need to get out of here."

14
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.341
Tom quietly opened the door, and a servant sprang to his feet.

15
00:01:20.361 --> 00:01:25.423
"Your Highness, may I help—" Tom slammed the door shut.

16
00:01:25.443 --> 00:01:29.504
"That servant thinks I'm Prince Edward!"

17
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.603
Before he could decide what to do next, there was a knock at the door.

18
00:01:36.823 --> 00:01:39.966
The same servant entered and announced, "Lady Jane."

19
00:01:43.308 --> 00:01:46.050
A girl in a beautiful dress ran toward Tom.

20
00:01:47.331 --> 00:01:49.733
But she stopped short when Tom fell to his knees.

21
00:01:49.753 --> 00:01:52.635
"What's wrong, Your Highness?"

22
00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:53.596
she said.

23
00:01:53.616 --> 00:01:55.737
"Have mercy on me!"

24
00:01:56.137 --> 00:01:56.898
Tom cried.

25
00:01:56.918 --> 00:02:02.081
"I'm not the prince, but only Tom Canty from Offal Street.

26
00:02:03.401 --> 00:02:06.142
Please help me find the prince and return these clothes to him.

27
00:02:07.062 --> 00:02:09.783
Then I'll be on my way and won't trouble any of you again."

28
00:02:09.803 --> 00:02:13.944
"You shouldn't be on your knees, my cousin."

29
00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:16.545
Lady Jane was horrified.

30
00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:19.466
"I should be bowing to you."

31
00:02:22.587 --> 00:02:25.808
She fled the room, which only increased Tom's panic.

32
00:02:28.024 --> 00:02:28.764
"What should I do?

33
00:02:29.325 --> 00:02:30.185
What should I do?"

34
00:02:30.665 --> 00:02:32.226
he repeated, pacing the floor.

35
00:02:34.727 --> 00:02:37.908
Meanwhile the servant told another servant what he had seen.

36
00:02:37.928 --> 00:02:42.310
"Prince Edward is behaving very strangely and doesn't think he's a prince!"

37
00:02:48.952 --> 00:02:53.194
The news spread rapidly throughout the palace until it reached King Henry.

38
00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:57.496
"The poor boy must be ill," he said.

39
00:02:59.424 --> 00:03:04.886
King Henry immediately issued an order that all talk about Prince Edward's illness must stop.

40
00:03:06.126 --> 00:03:08.567
Anyone who disobeyed would be put to death.

41
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:12.608
Then he asked for Prince Edward to be brought to him.

42
00:03:16.169 --> 00:03:20.890
Tom didn't understand where Lord Hertford, the prince's chief adviser, was leading him.

43
00:03:23.651 --> 00:03:26.112
They walked down one long corridor after another.

44
00:03:28.236 --> 00:03:32.217
Finally, they entered a grand room, where an old man was lying on a couch.

45
00:03:34.218 --> 00:03:36.418
He sat up and beckoned for Tom to approach.

46
00:03:36.438 --> 00:03:40.859
"My dear son, are you ill?"

47
00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:41.680
he said.

48
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.661
"Or are you playing a joke on your father, the king?"

49
00:03:48.301 --> 00:03:50.022
Tom instantly dropped to his knees.

50
00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:52.562
"You're King Henry?

51
00:03:53.603 --> 00:03:54.963
Then I'm in real trouble."

52
00:03:54.983 --> 00:04:02.473
"Oh dear, I'd hoped the rumors about your illness weren't true," the king said.

53
00:04:02.493 --> 00:04:05.534
"But this is worse than I'd expected.

54
00:04:05.974 --> 00:04:06.414
Come here."

55
00:04:08.895 --> 00:04:12.236
Trembling, Tom went and stood in front of King Henry.

56
00:04:12.256 --> 00:04:18.097
"Prince Edward, tell me that you recognize your father," the king said.

57
00:04:21.298 --> 00:04:22.618
Tom took a deep breath.

58
00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:27.520
"I hope that you'll believe me, Your Majesty, but I'm not Prince Edward.

59
00:04:29.064 --> 00:04:32.027
I'm only one of your subjects from the poorest part of the city.

60
00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:34.749
Please don't send me to prison.

61
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.692
I'm too young to spend the rest of my life there."

62
00:04:38.712 --> 00:04:43.076
"Send my son to prison?

63
00:04:44.337 --> 00:04:46.639
Don't be ridiculous," the king said.

64
00:04:48.281 --> 00:04:50.462
Tom was relieved but still uncertain.

65
00:04:50.482 --> 00:04:52.824
"Then I'm free to go?"

66
00:04:52.844 --> 00:04:55.186
"Go where?"

67
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:56.668
King Henry asked.

68
00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.740
"Home, Your Majesty."

69
00:05:01.821 --> 00:05:04.322
Baffled, the king turned to Lord Hertford.

70
00:05:04.342 --> 00:05:06.862
"What do you think is the matter?"

71
00:05:06.882 --> 00:05:13.164
"Perhaps only part of the prince's mind is confused.

72
00:05:14.604 --> 00:05:20.866
Your Majesty could ask him about something other than yourself," Lord Hertford suggested.

73
00:05:22.527 --> 00:05:25.527
King Henry nodded and asked Tom a question in Latin.

74
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.141
With some hesitation, Tom responded correctly.

75
00:05:31.161 --> 00:05:33.902
"Excellent!" the king said.

76
00:05:33.922 --> 00:05:36.062
"Now try this."

77
00:05:37.502 --> 00:05:41.083
He asked another question in French.

78
00:05:41.103 --> 00:05:49.266
"I'm sorry," Tom said, "but I don't even know what language you're speaking."

79
00:05:52.066 --> 00:05:53.267
King Henry frowned.

80
00:05:53.287 --> 00:06:00.112
"Too much studying has obviously caused this problem, Lord Hertford!

81
00:06:00.152 --> 00:06:02.875
No more lessons for Prince Edward until his health returns.

82
00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:09.960
In the meantime," he said to Tom, "what have you done with the Great Seal?"

83
00:06:11.782 --> 00:06:12.743
"The Great Seal?"

84
00:06:13.163 --> 00:06:14.764
Tom asked, confused.

85
00:06:14.784 --> 00:06:19.068
"Yes, you wanted to look at it last week.

86
00:06:20.769 --> 00:06:24.592
But I need it so I can place my seal on the death warrant of the Duke of

87
00:06:24.652 --> 00:06:28.936
Norfolk. I would like my enemy to die before I do."

88
00:06:31.448 --> 00:06:32.469
Tom bit his lip.

89
00:06:32.489 --> 00:06:36.633
"I have no idea where it is—or what it is."

90
00:06:40.756 --> 00:06:45.200
Your Majesty could use the Small Seal," Lord Hertford suggested.

91
00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.463
"Yes, yes, I know that."

92
00:06:50.304 --> 00:06:52.706
King Henry seemed tired and impatient.

93
00:06:53.947 --> 00:06:54.508
"Please leave."

94
00:06:58.516 --> 00:07:01.418
Lord Hertford signaled for Tom to bow to the king.

95
00:07:01.438 --> 00:07:07.561
"I'm a prisoner in this palace," Tom thought.

96
00:07:07.582 --> 00:07:10.964
"And I'll never be set free!"
